    "sha": "cfef8048f9ad7a96a8751e41ff7fa0428fcb3a16",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVVonwNoAKGNmZWY4MDQ4ZjlhZDdhOTZhODc1MWU0MWZmN2ZhMDQyOGZjYjNhMTY",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "168627+NeoTech@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2026-11-26T10:18:13Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "168627+NeoTech@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2026-11-26T10:18:13Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(pathkernel): one region model for selection, material side and bounds\n\nStage 1 of the path kernel (K1). `region(sel, material, bounds, plane,\ntool, leave)` builds one region value from a selection, the material\nside and the bounds. The material side is a parameter of its own, and\nno start side reaches the region.\n\n- `Selection` and `Chain`: an edge, a face, a chain or points that\n  straight lines join, valid by construction. Each degenerate selection\n  is refused by name (empty, short, not finite, repeated point, no area,\n  self-crossing, two chains that cross).\n- `PlanarRegion` holds its work plane and checks that its part walls and\n  stock edges partition the boundary of the centre, and that the loops\n  are oriented by their nesting.\n- The adapter in camcraft-motion (`machining2d/kernel_region.rs`) maps\n  the present carriers (a picked area, Contour `Side`, `StartSide`) onto\n  the kernel inputs. No old planner calls it: the output does not change.\n- Pins: one selection gives one region through the Pocket, Contour and\n  pocket-carrier paths; two present disagreements (the Offset band at the\n  stock edge, the Pocket sliver filter) are pinned and recorded in\n  docs/decisions/4025-kernel-region.md.\n\nRefs #4025\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
